<title>USA: Thomas &amp; Betts Q3 shr rises to $0.64.</title>
<headline>Thomas &amp; Betts Q3 shr rises to $0.64.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.64		    $0.53</p>
<p> Net			 25,822		   21,263</p>
<p> Sales		    351,211		  298,305</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  40,412		   39,973</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call consensus estimate was $0.63.  </p>
<p>Nine months</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.70		    $1.44</p>
<p> Net			 68,668		   57,610</p>
<p> Sales		  1,042,288		  896,935</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  40,300		   39,934</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: For 1996, outbound freight expense was reclassified from marketing, general and administrative expenses to a contra sales item. 1995 amounts were restated to conform. 1995 amounts restated to include the 1995 acquisitions of Catamount Manufacturing Inc and E.K. Campbell Co, accounted as a pooling of interests.</p>
